  "notes": "MCA/Silas then Epic adult-R&B soprano with a So So Def remix identity, 1992–2003. The research gives \"56–101; ballads 56–82 half-time\", so the ballad band is the base with `halfTime` true; the ~101 remix is the entry's \"second commercial identity\", a re-bedding of the same vocal rather than a second grammar, and is not folded in. Three drum deltas from \"Dupri-style dry kit at the low tempo, clap on 3\": one or two kicks a bar with syncopation at 0.11, a clap stacked on beat 3 with `offGridMs` 0 and almost no ghost activity, and a non-continuous 16th hat at 0.13 fill density — the So So Def dryness, distinguished from Xscape's by a slightly higher hat floor and a rim/shaker perc pair. Harmony is \"4-chord maj7/m9 cycles\", so the triad share is 0.12 and the families run four deep. The identifying melodic parameter is range: \"whistle-register ad-libs and long sustained top notes are the identity, with 2–3 voice thin harmony\" — a melody ceiling at MIDI 98, the highest in this section, with a legato articulation, a 0.14 octave-jump probability and a counter density of only 0.24. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ The mode of 66 is INFERRED — the entry gives sourced points at 56 and 82 but no centre — as are every velocity, density and register number. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"major-mode with jazz extensions [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
